                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I was going through a bunch of old games in my Steam Library; a lot were terrible games I got from old Humble Bundle codes, but this one was actually not bad. It's genuinely kind of fun and has a decently interesting gimmick and presentation. Really, the only issue was that the controls were kind of clunky, but maybe it was because I was using a keyboard and a controller might be better. I mean, I've played better puzzle games, even some with a similar mechanic to this, but it's still not bad. I only played about the first 10 levels since I'm just trying to go through a bunch of games, but I might actually return to this some other time. For all I know, the quality could go downhill, but from what I played, I think I got a good enough gist of the game.",
